/E (The interpretation of the result \(for models trained using IPC sections\) are made assuming the IPCs are independent. So considering that, we are able find out pattern from the data that few IPCs are always coming into picture for discriminating the Bail and No Bail files.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
534 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 975 0 R
/E (However we can also see that many times bail files are getting misclassified as No Bail, which might be because of, in practical scenario, many cases with serious charges like 420 \(No Bailable\) 376 \(rape\), which would have been generally in No bail files, are also getting Bail.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
535 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 976 0 R
/E (This practically make sense as even if the charges are serious, but if the accuse have enough evidence they get bail easily, but as our models are solely dependent on IPCs, it is decreasing the power of our model in discrimination. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
